# EDGE-LOG cloud runner environment -- FILL-IN-THE-BLANKS reference.
#
# install.sh writes a real ~/edgelog/edgelog.env for you (with the paths already
# filled in for your VM) and never overwrites it once it exists -- you normally never
# copy this file by hand. It's kept here so every variable the stack can read is in
# ONE place with a plain-language explanation, for when you want to add or change one
# yourself (e.g. sizing EDGELOG_VALIDATE_WORKERS for a bigger VM shape, or moving
# NTFY_TOPIC). No secrets or real values below -- CHANGE-ME / example paths only.
#
# After editing the REAL edgelog.env: sudo systemctl restart edgelog-runner.service
# edgelog-qqq-exec.service (both read the same file).

# ── base paths ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The one folder api/qqq_exec.py and api/webull_orders.py build every OTHER default
# path from (qqq_exec output, webull keys/tokens, order-adapter state) when a more
# specific variable below isn't set. install.sh sets this to $HOME/edgelog.
EDGELOG_HOME=/home/ubuntu/edgelog
# Server timezone -- keep this America/New_York so log timestamps and the session-
# window rails (09:30-16:00 etc.) read the same as on the owner's PC.
TZ=America/New_York

# ── which host is this (2026-09-13 cross-host lease) ────────────────────────────────
# Tells the QQQ shadow adapter it is the CLOUD copy: the phone tab's "running on" shows
# CLOUD, and the lease guard (LEASE_STALE_SEC / api/qqq_exec.py's _check_lease) uses it
# to refuse to serve while the OTHER host's heartbeat is still fresh, so the PC and this
# VM can never both trade the account at once. Set to "cloud" here; leave UNSET on the PC.
EDGELOG_HOST_ROLE=cloud
# Optional override for the lease's host identity (default: the OS hostname, which is
# normally enough since there are only ever two candidates -- the PC and this VM).
# EDGELOG_HOST_ID=CHANGE-ME-only-if-hostnames-collide

# ── Firebase (job queue + Firestore status doc) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Firebase Admin SDK service-account key -- copied by push_secrets.ps1, never in git.
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/EDGE-LOG/serviceAccount.json

# ── Webull LIVE (existing key -- api/webull_sync.py's daily trade-history pull, and
# the live order path if the owner ever arms LIVE) ──────────────────────────────────
EDGELOG_WEBULL_KEYS=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/webull_keys.json
EDGELOG_WEBULL_TOKEN_DIR=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/webull_token

# ── Webull ORDER adapter (api/webull_orders.py) -- flip PAPER on here ───────────────
# Mode itself is NOT an env var -- it's the "mode" field in the JSON file named by
# EDGELOG_WEBULL_ORDERS_CONFIG below (OFF by default; see README.md "Webull ORDER
# adapter"). The env vars here only say WHERE that config/state/creds live.
# SEPARATE sandbox app key/secret -- never the live webull_keys.json contents.
EDGELOG_WEBULL_PAPER_KEYS=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/webull_paper_keys.json
EDGELOG_WEBULL_PAPER_TOKEN_DIR=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/webull_paper_token
# {"mode": "OFF"|"PAPER"|"LIVE", "rails": {...}} -- create this file yourself to flip
# modes; it does not exist until you make it, which is what keeps the default OFF.
EDGELOG_WEBULL_ORDERS_CONFIG=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/webull_orders/config.json
# Idempotency/rails/reconcile state -- the adapter's own memory across restarts.
EDGELOG_WEBULL_ORDERS_STATE=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/webull_orders/state.json
# Touch this file (any content) to flatten every order-adapter position and block new
# entries -- the adapter's kill switch, independent of the shadow book's own KILL file.
EDGELOG_WEBULL_ORDERS_KILL=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/webull_orders/KILL
# Must exist AND config.json must say "mode":"LIVE" before a single real order is
# placed -- neither is created by install.sh or by any Claude session, ever.
EDGELOG_WEBULL_ARM_LIVE=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/webull_orders/ARM_LIVE

# ── QQQ shadow adapter (api/qqq_exec.py) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where its own orders.csv/trades.csv/broker_orders.csv/state.json/config.json/KILL live.
EDGELOG_QQQ_EXEC_DIR=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/qqq_exec
# 10-second NQ bar feed the shadow book falls back to ONLY in "ninjatrader" signal-source
# mode (default is "engine", which never reads these -- see api/qqq_exec.py's module
# docstring). Left pointing at paths that won't exist on this VM; harmless while
# signal_source stays "engine".
EDGELOG_NQ_10S_PRIMARY=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/ohlc_addon/NQ_10s.csv
EDGELOG_NQ_10S_FALLBACK=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/ohlc/NQ_10s.csv

# ── job-runner tuning ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fold-level parallelism inside one validate (augur_engine.wf_pool). Keep at or below
# the box's OCPU count -- 2 for the recommended 2-OCPU/12GB Always Free shape.
EDGELOG_VALIDATE_WORKERS=2
# Reuses cached trial results across re-searches of the same region (see
# BACKTEST_SPEED.md) -- leave on.
AUGUR_TRIAL_CACHE=1

# ── alerts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ntfy.sh push topic for edgelog-healthcheck.service and the runner's own alerters
# (api/nt_exec_review.py, api/nt_drawdown_alert.py). Reuse the topic already set on the
# PC (tools/_restart_runner.bat.example) so alerts land on the same phone, or pick a
# fresh name at https://ntfy.sh -- anyone who learns the topic name can read the
# messages, so treat it like a lightly-kept secret, not a public channel.
NTFY_TOPIC=CHANGE-ME

# ── NinjaTrader / PC-only (leave UNSET on this VM) ──────────────────────────────────
# These exist for api/nt_sync.py, api/data_health.py, api/nt_drawdown_alert.py,
# api/nt_exec_review.py and read files only NinjaTrader on the PC ever writes. There is
# no NinjaTrader on this VM (see README.md "What runs where") -- setting these here
# would just point at paths that never get created; leaving them unset makes those
# side-duties log "not present" and skip, which is correct on this box.
# EDGELOG_NT_FILLS=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/fills.csv
# EDGELOG_NT_OHLC=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/ohlc
# EDGELOG_DD_STATE=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/dd_alert_state.json
# EDGELOG_EXEC_REVIEW_STATE=/home/ubuntu/edgelog/seen_executions.json
